      "label": "text",
      "prov": [],
      "orig": "The entropy of a distribution $y$ is the expected number of bits under the optimal code, with $\\log \\frac{1}{y_i}$ bits for the $i$-th symbol:",
      "text": "The entropy of a distribution $y$ is the expected number of bits under the optimal code, with $\\log \\frac{1}{y_i}$ bits for the $i$-th symbol:"
    },
    {
      "self_ref": "#/texts/3",
      "parent": {
        "$ref": "#/body"
      },
      "children": [],
      "content_layer": "body",
      "label": "formula",
      "prov": [],
      "orig": "H(y) = \\sum_i y_i \\log \\frac{1}{y_i} = -\\sum_i y_i \\log y_i",
      "text": "H(y) = \\sum_i y_i \\log \\frac{1}{y_i} = -\\sum_i y_i \\log y_i"
    },
    {
      "self_ref": "#/texts/4",
      "parent": {
        "$ref": "#/body"
      },
      "children": [],
      "content_layer": "body",
      "label": "text",
      "prov": [],
      "orig": "Encoding symbols from $y$ with the wrong tool $\\hat{y}$ costs more; the cost is $0.10 per bit and $5 per message.",
      "text": "Encoding symbols from $y$ with the wrong tool $\\hat{y}$ costs more; the cost is $0.10 per bit and $5 per message."
    },
    {
      "self_ref": "#/texts/5",
      "parent": {
        "$ref": "#/body"
      },
      "children": [],
      "content_layer": "body",
      "label": "section_header",
      "prov": [],
      "orig": "KL divergence",
      "text": "KL divergence",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "self_ref": "#/texts/6",
      "parent": {
